# Enforce LF line endings for all text files
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files require CRLF
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# ⭐ THE TREND LOG IS APPEND-ONLY, AND EVERY RUNG APPENDS AT THE SAME ANCHOR.
# `ScaleHistory` inserts each row immediately before that table's
# `<!-- scale-history:… -->` end marker, and there are three such tables — so any two
# rungs landing in sequence conflict three times, every time, on rows that do not
# overlap in meaning at all. Measured: six such conflicts in one session, each one
# costing a full ~13-minute gate battery re-run because `rung-finish.sh` rebases first.
# `union` keeps both sides' rows, which is the resolution a human performs by hand
# every time. VERIFIED for BOTH merge and rebase before this line was committed — the
# rebase case is the one that matters, because `rung-finish.sh` rebases onto origin/main
# before it gates, and a scripted auto-resolve written for it turned out to be redundant.
#
# ⚠ UNION APPLIES TO THE WHOLE FILE, so two agents EDITING THE SAME EXISTING ROW get
# BOTH versions kept rather than a conflict. That is not hypothetical — rows do get
# edited in place (a re-measurement corrected on the row it belongs to). The failure is
# a visibly duplicated row carrying the same date and rung name, not silent corruption,
# which is why it is acceptable HERE and must not be extended to source.
docs/optimization-log.md merge=union

# ⭐ THE fmt ORACLE IS BYTES, SO GIT MUST NOT NORMALIZE IT.
# `tests/fmt/fixtures/**` and `tests/fmt/selftest-cases/**` hold a formatter's REAL
# OUTPUT, compared byte for byte by `tests/fmt/fixtures.test.maxon`. Under the
# `* text=auto eol=lf` rule above, git would rewrite line endings on checkout — so on a
# host where `fmt` emitted CRLF the harness would be comparing against a file git had
# silently converted, and the corpus would agree with a formatter it had never seen.
# Nothing is broken today (both compilers emit LF); this makes the oracle inert on that
# axis, which is the same reason nothing in it is stored as a live `.maxon`.
tests/fmt/fixtures/** -text
tests/fmt/selftest-cases/** -text
